<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ============================================================================
     MapControlsStrip — the map's tools and the radar-site picker, ON the map instead of two clicks deep in Settings.
     It is the CONTENT of the bottom chrome's upper tier: MainWindow drops it into an OverlayBar
     (IsRaised, ShowTab=False, EdgeStyle=CastShadow) that supplies the surface, the EDGE and the
     padding, exactly the way RadarControls is content for the bar below it.

       ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░   ← shadow, thrown onto the map

       ╭─ ˅ Tools ─╮ ╭─ ˅ Bar ─╮                                    ← MainWindow's shared rail
       ┌──────────────────────────────┐
       │ ⌂ KTLX  Oklahoma City      ● │  ← PINNED: home            (the site picker's dropdown, opening UP)
       │──────────────────────────────│
       │ ★ KINX  Tulsa              ● │  ← favorites, starred order, scrolls
       │ ★ KFWS  Dallas/Ft Worth    ● │     ● = online / offline / grey not-checked
       │──────────────────────────────│
       │ Open Atlas                   │  ← footer (+ a hint line above it when there are no sites)
       └──────────────────────────────┘          ┌─────────────────────────────┐
                                                  │ Moore, OK          pop 62k  │   ← place suggestions
                                                  └─────────────────────────────┘
                                                                                             ┌ Map layers ──────┐
                                                                                             │ ☑ Land           │
                                                                                             │ ☑ Water          │
                                                                                             │ ☑ Roads          │  ← the CAR's flyout
                                                                                             │ ☑ Buildings      │
                                                                                             │ ☑ Borders        │
                                                                                             │ ☐ Counties (grey)│  ← greyed unless the
                                                                                             │ ☑ Place names    │     style has county lines
                                                                                             │ Dim ──●───── 30% │
                                                                                             └──────────────────┘
       (◗)(✈)(⚗) [⌂ KTLX  Oklahoma City   ˅] (⌸) (◎)  (▣) [Search places  ⌕] (⊚) status   [▢][▥][▦] (⌘) (⛶) (▥|▴) [Isolate State ▾]   ← THIS
        ↑ LEFT = RADAR + MAP: show each    ↑ CENTER = where; the box is          ↑ RIGHT = MAP ONLY: pane layout
          network's sites (NEXRAD /          CENTERED on the tier                  (1/2/4, current one LIT, accent
          TDWR / research), pick one (over the
          console, which answers when),    ▣ marker viewer — a PLACEHOLDER         cell = pane 0), reset north,
          ⌸ the RANGE RULER, then ◎ the    ⊚ Location (lit = your marker is out)   fit to view, MAP key + car, isolation
          RANGE RINGS on/off (lit = showing)
       ▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒   ← …and onto the bar: NO rule
       ◉  ⌕  ══ scrubber ══   ◀▶▶            ▤  ⊚  📡  ⚙           ← the bar
     ═══════════════════════ window bottom ═══════════════════════

     ⚠️ THERE IS NO LINE ANYWHERE ON THIS TIER. Its top edge throws a shadow onto the map and the
     bar below draws the band it receives from this one's underside. A hairline under a shadow reads
     as a seam someone forgot to finish - the two are alternatives, not layers.

     ⚠️ IT ALIGNS TO THE BAR'S CLUSTERS, not to itself, and the SIDES MEAN SOMETHING. LEFT sits over the
     radar console, so it holds the control that changes WHICH radar you are looking at (the console below
     answers WHEN). RIGHT sits over the window keys and holds the tools that touch ONLY the map — pane
     layout, reset north, fit to view, isolation — none of which loads or changes radar data. A new tool
     goes on the side whose question it answers. Both tiers carry the same 16px side padding so the two
     rows line up; that alignment is why the tools need no container of their own to look placed.

     ⚠️ HISTORY: this was a content-sized ISLAND that floated above the bar with a NOTCH cut in its
     underside, so the bar's pull-tab could rise through it. That shape is gone, and with it went a
     path builder, an equal-sides invariant that was correctness rather than cosmetics, three shared
     tab constants and a standing rule against ever giving this control a Background. Don't
     reintroduce the notch: see docs/ui-bottom-bar.md for what it cost and why the tab moved instead.

     ⚠️ ITS HOVER IS THE RAISED PAIR, and that is not a detail. A control resting on the raised
     surface cannot hover to OverlayBarSurfaceHoverBrush — in dark the raised ground (#141414) is
     already past it (#1A1A1A), so the hover would be invisible; in light it would go the wrong way.
     Each tier hovers one step further from its OWN ground.

     PLACE SEARCH sits in the CENTER, on the tier's exact midpoint (a [*, Auto, *] grid, the same trick as the
     bar's temporal pills below it); its status text hangs off the box's right in the third column so a
     message never pushes the box off-center. Typing shows
     GAZETTEER rows (offline); Enter/a row flies there and drops the search pin (MarkersViewModel).
     ⚠️ ONLINE (Nominatim) runs ONLY on Enter when the gazetteer found nothing — its policy forbids
     autocomplete. Don't wire it to TextChanged. ⚠️ Clearing the box removes the pin; that is the remove.
     ⚠️ Text is ONE-WAY from PlaceSearch.QueryText: picking a PastCast saved event pins the town it is named
     for through the SAME pin and puts the name in this box, so the box's X clears that pin too.
     ⚠️ An AutoSuggestBox is safe here (the wheel hazard is a CLOSED ComboBox cycling its selection).
     ⚠️ No Ctrl+F: the WebView owns keyboard focus once the map is clicked, so an accelerator here
     would work only sometimes.

     THE SEARCH IS FLANKED: marker viewer LEFT (a placeholder), LOCATION RIGHT. Both sit in the star
     columns hugging the box, so neither shifts it off the midpoint. Location moved here from the bar's
     right cluster — it is a "where on the map" move like search, and an occasional one.
     ⚠️ LOCATION LATCHES: as a plain button it would be a one-way door (nothing else in the shipped UI
     removes the marker — the Selected Marker window is pending re-add). Lit = your marker is out; clicking
     it lit removes it. ⚠️ IsChecked is ONE-WAY and re-asserted after the await in the handler: the locate
     can FAIL without any property changing, so nothing else would pull the toggle back down. Don't make
     it TwoWay. The tooltip carries "Locating…" / "Location unavailable" — a failure is otherwise silent.
     ⚠️ Its mark is a DRAWN reticle (PathIcon, 18-unit box), the same family as the on-map marker — a key
     pictures what it drops. That is why the bar's Inspect key is a magnifier; don't give it a reticle.
     ⚠️ The viewer's mark is a drawn TEARDROP, the search pin's shape. Its button has NO Click on purpose;
     wire it when the marker window exists (open bool + WindowManager registration — CLAUDE.md "Add a window").

     SITE MARKERS, LEFT EDGE — THREE toggles, one per network: ◗ NEXRAD (Radar.ShowNexradSites) · ✈ TDWR
     (ShowTdwrs) · ⚗ research (ShowResearchRadars), all TwoWay and PERSISTED. They sit here because showing the
     sites and picking one are the same question (WHICH radar).
     ⚠️ LIT = THAT NETWORK'S KEYS ARE SHOWING. The mark is fixed (it names the network, the on-map key's own
     glyph); the TOOLTIP speaks for the click ("Hide TDWR airport radars on the map").
     ⚠️ MAP MARKERS ONLY: they never remove a site from the Atlas or the site picker, and never unload a loop.
     ⚠️ NO MASTER: the old "hide all sites" eye is gone (2026-09-26) — all three off = no keys. The TDWR and
     research toggles moved here from Settings → Radar, where they used to switch those networks off app-wide.
     ⚠️ The words say "radar sites", NEVER "markers": ▣ below is the MARKER viewer (search pins, your location).

     SITE PICKER, LEFT — home + favorite radar sites (RadarSiteFavoritesViewModel). It replaced TWO doors to
     one list: the bar's Home key, and the side car on the bar's Atlas key (whose flyout this dropdown absorbed).
     The FACE is the site on the map now: ⌂ when it is home, ★ when a favorite, bare otherwise (a site loaded
     from a marker is still named, with no row lit). Home is the PINNED section, so going home is two clicks.
     ⚠️ A pick ACTS through ItemPicked, NOT SelectedItem: picking the site already loaded must still fly back to
     it, and that changes no property. SelectedItem is ONE-WAY from LoadedSite and re-asserted after the pick
     (a refused pick would otherwise leave the face naming a site that never loaded).
     ⚠️ DISABLED in PastCast (a pick would re-target the replay); the tooltip sits on a WRAPPER so it still
     explains itself — WinUI shows no tooltip on a disabled control.
     ⚠️ The face has a FIXED width so a long name never resizes the tier; the name trims.
     ⚠️ Glyphs E80F (Home) / E735 (FavoriteStarFill) are NOT verified by rendering in the real font.

     PANE LAYOUT sits RIGHT, first of the map tools: THREE toggles (1 / 2 / 4), the current one lit.
     It stays with the map tools even though each pane carries its own radar product: what THIS control
     changes is how the map is split. What each pane shows is chosen in its notch (PaneNotchContent). It moved
     here from the bar, where it was one wide key that cycled and drew the NEXT layout — three toggles show
     the current layout and reach any layout in one click, which the cycling key could do neither of.
     ⚠️ ONE-WAY IsChecked + re-assert in OnPaneLayoutClick: clicking the LIT toggle sets the layout it already
     is (no property change), and the toggle would otherwise un-light itself. Every layout is an on-state.
     ⚠️ SQUARE marks (18×18), NOT the map band's 26:14 shape: at 32 px a wide quad mark's cells were ~10×5
     and read as a smudge (mocked up and rejected). Solid blocks with 2 px gaps, not outlines — small solid
     shapes stay distinct where hairlines merge. Accent cell = pane 0 (left; bottom-left in quad), as on the map.
     Drawn Rectangles with fixed theme brushes — Shapes don't inherit the template's Foreground.
     Tooltips read "Activate N-pane mode". No "two stacked": weather reads left-to-right across a storm.

     MAP sits RIGHT, beside state isolation — both take parts of the map away (Basemap = BasemapViewModel).
     The KEY hides the whole basemap: a blank, THEME-coloured ground (theme.css anvil-map-blank) under the overlays,
     for screenshots / thumbnails / a clean storm. LIT = THE MAP IS SHOWING (default lit); the tooltip speaks
     for the click. The CAR opens the layer flyout: which basemap GROUPS draw, and a dimmer (0-90%) that fades
     the basemap toward blank. ⚠️ Hiding OVERRIDES the ticks without changing them — show again and your set
     returns (the flyout says so while hidden). ⚠️ The hide is SESSION-ONLY; ticks + dimmer persist.
     ⚠️ A pair, not SplitTemporalToggle: that is a 72 px bar key; this tier's tools are 32 px.

     Host contract: ViewModel (MapViewModel). Add a tool = one Button in the panel of the side it belongs to.
     ============================================================================ -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.MapControlsStrip"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             xmlns:vm="using:Anvil.ViewModels"
             xmlns:models="using:Anvil.Models"
             xmlns:conv="using:Anvil.Converters"
             xmlns:comp="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <conv:SiteAvailabilityToBrushConverter x:Key="AvailabilityToBrush"/>

        <!-- A tool button. LOCAL, not in Styles.xaml: this strip is its only consumer, which is that
             file's house rule. Deliberately NOT the bar-key chain — a bar key is a 72px square carrying
             a mark over a NAME, and a row of those would make this a second bar rather than a tier of
             tools. Minimal template so it stays opaque in every state and cannot pick up the stock
             button's chrome. -->
        <Style x:Key="StripToolButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Width" Value="32"/>
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="32"/>
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="5"/>
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                        <Grid x:Name="Root"
                              Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                              BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                              BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                              CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                            <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                </VisualStateGroup>
                            </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="Glyph"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"/>
                        </Grid>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <!-- The LATCHING tool (Location): StripToolButtonStyle's look plus the bar's lit vocabulary — accent
             BORDER + Elevated face while checked (Elevated is "a control that is ON", never a tier). A separate
             style because a Button style can't target a ToggleButton. -->
        <Style x:Key="StripToolToggleStyle" TargetType="ToggleButton">
            <Setter Property="Width" Value="32"/>
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="32"/>
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent"/>
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1"/>
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="5"/>
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="ToggleButton">
                        <Grid x:Name="Root"
                              Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                              BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                              BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                              CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                            <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Normal"/>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultSolidBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Checked">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPointerOver">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceRaisedHoverBrush}"/>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="CheckedPressed">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.Background" Value="{ThemeResource OverlayBarSurfaceElevatedBrush}"/>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="CheckedDisabled">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Root.BorderBrush" Value="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}"/>
                                            <Setter Target="Glyph.Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorDisabledBrush}"/>
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                </VisualStateGroup>
                            </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="Glyph"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"/>
                        </Grid>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <!-- One isolation row, for BOTH sections of the picker. The modes carry hover text; the places
             have a null Tooltip, which shows nothing rather than an empty box. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="IsolationRowTemplate" x:DataType="vm:StateIsolationOption">
            <Grid Background="Transparent" ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind Tooltip}">
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Label}" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
            </Grid>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- One site-picker ROW (both sections): pin mark, id, name, availability dot. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="SiteRowTemplate" x:DataType="vm:RadarSiteRow">
            <Grid ColumnSpacing="10">
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="16"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="14" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                          Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                          Glyph="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.PinGlyph(IsHome, IsFavorite), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{x:Bind Id}" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Bind Name}" FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                <Ellipse Grid.Column="3" Width="8" Height="8" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         Fill="{x:Bind Availability, Converter={StaticResource AvailabilityToBrush}, Mode=OneWay}"/>
            </Grid>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- The site picker's FACE: the pin mark (collapsed for a site that is neither), id and name — no dot.
             No foregrounds set: the text inherits the picker's, so it greys with it in PastCast. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="SiteFaceTemplate" x:DataType="vm:RadarSiteRow">
            <!-- A Grid, not a horizontal StackPanel: only a * column gives the name a width to trim to.
                 Gaps are MARGINS, not ColumnSpacing, so a collapsed mark leaves no gap behind. -->
            <Grid>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <FontIcon Margin="0,0,8,0"
                          FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="14" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                          Glyph="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.PinGlyph(IsHome, IsFavorite), Mode=OneWay}"
                          Visibility="{x:Bind comp:MapControlsStrip.PinVisibility(IsHome, IsFavorite), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Margin="0,0,8,0" Text="{x:Bind Id}" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{x:Bind Name}" VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"/>
            </Grid>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- One place-search row: the name left, population (or the OpenStreetMap credit) right. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="PlaceRowTemplate" x:DataType="models:PlaceResult">
            <Grid ColumnSpacing="12">
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Display}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{x:Bind Detail}" FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
            </Grid>
        </DataTemplate>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <!-- ⚠️ NO Background here: the OverlayBar hosting this tier paints the raised surface, and a second
         opaque fill would be one more place the tier's colour is written. One cell, three children — the
         tools hug the window edges the bar's own clusters hug, and place search holds the center. -->
    <Grid>
        <!-- ===== RADAR SITES — LEFT, over the radar console (see the header): show them, pick one ===== -->
        <StackPanel x:Name="LeftTools"
                    Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <!-- SITE MARKERS — one plain TwoWay toggle per network (a click always changes the flag, so no
                 re-assert). The marks are the on-map keys' own network glyphs (radar-sites.js CLASS_GLYPH),
                 redrawn as FILLED geometry in the 18-unit box: a PathIcon only fills, and only a PathIcon takes the
                 key's lit / unlit foreground (a stroked Path wouldn't). The sweep's and the flask's strokes became
                 2-unit bands with round caps; F1 = nonzero fill, so the flask's neck bar and body don't cancel. -->
            <ToggleButton x:Name="NexradSitesToggle"
                          Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowNexradSites, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind SitesTooltip(ViewModel.Radar.ShowNexradSites, 'NEXRAD radar sites'), Mode=OneWay}">
                <PathIcon Data="M2.9,13.5 A1.6,1.6 0 1 1 6.1,13.5 A1.6,1.6 0 1 1 2.9,13.5 Z M4.5,8 A5.5,5.5 0 0 1 10,13.5 A1,1 0 0 1 8,13.5 A3.5,3.5 0 0 0 4.5,10 A1,1 0 0 1 4.5,8 Z M4.5,3 A10.5,10.5 0 0 1 15,13.5 A1,1 0 0 1 13,13.5 A8.5,8.5 0 0 0 4.5,5 A1,1 0 0 1 4.5,3 Z"/>
            </ToggleButton>
            <ToggleButton x:Name="TdwrSitesToggle"
                          Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowTdwrs, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind SitesTooltip(ViewModel.Radar.ShowTdwrs, 'TDWR airport radars'), Mode=OneWay}">
                <PathIcon Data="M9,0.9 C9.54,0.9 9.9,1.71 9.9,2.7 V7.38 L16.2,10.98 V12.69 L9.9,10.89 V14.4 L11.7,15.75 V17.1 L9,16.2 L6.3,17.1 V15.75 L8.1,14.4 V10.89 L1.8,12.69 V10.98 L8.1,7.38 V2.7 C8.1,1.71 8.46,0.9 9,0.9 Z"/>
            </ToggleButton>
            <ToggleButton x:Name="ResearchSitesToggle"
                          Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowResearchRadars, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind SitesTooltip(ViewModel.Radar.ShowResearchRadars, 'research radars'), Mode=OneWay}">
                <PathIcon Data="F1 M6.75,2.25 A0.75,0.75 0 0 0 6.75,3.75 H11.25 A0.75,0.75 0 0 0 11.25,2.25 Z M6.75,3 V6.5625 L3.537,12.6225 A2.175,2.175 0 0 0 5.475,15.75 H12.525 A2.175,2.175 0 0 0 14.463,12.6225 L11.25,6.5625 V3 Z M8.25,3.75 H9.75 V6.9375 L13.137,13.3275 A0.675,0.675 0 0 1 12.525,14.25 H5.475 A0.675,0.675 0 0 1 4.863,13.3275 L8.25,6.9375 Z"/>
            </ToggleButton>

            <!-- SITE PICKER. The wrapper carries the tooltip (a disabled control shows none); Transparent so it
                 hit-tests. -->
            <Grid Background="Transparent"
                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.PickerToolTip, Mode=OneWay}">
                <prim:SectionedComboBox x:Name="SitePicker"
                                        Width="260"
                                        PlaceholderText="Radar site"
                                        PinnedItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.HomeSites, Mode=OneWay}"
                                        ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.FavoriteSites, Mode=OneWay}"
                                        SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.LoadedSite, Mode=OneWay}"
                                        ItemTemplate="{StaticResource SiteRowTemplate}"
                                        FaceTemplate="{StaticResource SiteFaceTemplate}"
                                        IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.CanPickSites, Mode=OneWay}"
                                        ItemPicked="OnSitePicked">
                    <prim:SectionedComboBox.FooterContent>
                        <StackPanel Spacing="4">
                            <TextBlock Margin="11,2,11,2"
                                       Text="Set a home site or star favorites in the Atlas to list them here."
                                       TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12"
                                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"
                                       Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.IsEmpty, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                            <Button HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalContentAlignment="Left"
                                    Background="Transparent" BorderThickness="0" Padding="11,6"
                                    Content="Open Atlas"
                                    Click="OnOpenAtlasClick"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </prim:SectionedComboBox.FooterContent>
                </prim:SectionedComboBox>
            </Grid>

            <!-- RANGE RULER - arm the graduated spoke from the loaded site out to the range ring. LEFT,
                 because what it measures against is RADAR (the ring is the data's own outer extent) and it
                 dies with the loop; the right cluster's tools touch only the map. Plain TwoWay: a click
                 always changes the mode, so there is nothing to re-assert.
                 ⚠️ Disabled with nothing on screen, so you cannot arm it onto an empty map - but a ruler armed
                 on a loop that then clears STAYS armed (lit and disabled) and draws itself again at the next
                 site, still on the bearing you left it. Sticky on purpose: measuring from each site in turn is
                 the gesture, so re-arming per site would be the annoyance. Unlike Inspect, which disarms.
                 The icon is a PathIcon, not a FontIcon: the same choice the Location reticle beside it made,
                 and it does not bet the control on an unverified Segoe glyph. -->
            <ToggleButton x:Name="RangeRulerToggle"
                          Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.HasRadarDisplay, Mode=OneWay}"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.IsRangeRulerOn, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="Range ruler - drag the bead to measure from the site (click again to turn it off)">
                <!-- A graduated bar: outer rect, hollowed, with four ticks hanging off its top edge
                     (EvenOdd puts the ticks back inside the hole). -->
                <PathIcon Data="M1,6 H17 V12 H1 Z M2.4,7.4 H15.6 V10.6 H2.4 Z M4.2,7.4 H5.0 V10.2 H4.2 Z M7.0,7.4 H7.8 V9.2 H7.0 Z M9.8,7.4 H10.6 V10.2 H9.8 Z M12.6,7.4 H13.4 V9.2 H12.6 Z"/>
            </ToggleButton>

            <!-- RANGE RINGS - the MASTER show/hide for every range ring, its labels and the label handle
                 (Radar.RangeRings.RingsVisible, PERSISTED). Beside the Ruler because they are one family: the
                 ruler ends on the ring. Plain TwoWay (a click always flips it). LIT = RINGS ARE SHOWING; the
                 tooltip speaks for the click. NOT disabled without a loop - it is a switch you can set ahead.
                 WHICH rings, and how they look, stay in Settings → Radar Range Ring (set-once).
                 The icon is a drawn PathIcon (three concentric rings round a centre dot, EvenOdd hollows them),
                 the same no-unverified-glyph choice as the Ruler's. -->
            <ToggleButton x:Name="RangeRingsToggle"
                          Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.RangeRings.RingsVisible, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind RangeRingsTooltip(ViewModel.Radar.RangeRings.RingsVisible), Mode=OneWay}">
                <PathIcon Data="M9,0.5 A8.5,8.5 0 1 0 9,17.5 A8.5,8.5 0 1 0 9,0.5 Z M9,1.9 A7.1,7.1 0 1 0 9,16.1 A7.1,7.1 0 1 0 9,1.9 Z M9,3.9 A5.1,5.1 0 1 0 9,14.1 A5.1,5.1 0 1 0 9,3.9 Z M9,5.3 A3.7,3.7 0 1 0 9,12.7 A3.7,3.7 0 1 0 9,5.3 Z M9,7.4 A1.6,1.6 0 1 0 9,10.6 A1.6,1.6 0 1 0 9,7.4 Z"/>
            </ToggleButton>
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- ===== PLACE SEARCH — CENTER =====
             A [*, Auto, *] grid spanning the tier puts the box on the exact midpoint. ⚠️ No Background on this
             Grid: a background-less Grid isn't hit-testable, so its empty star columns don't swallow clicks
             meant for the site picker or the map tools beneath them. -->
        <Grid>
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

            <!-- MARKER VIEWER — PLACEHOLDER. No Click until the marker window exists (see the header).
                 A teardrop with an eye, the search pin's own shape. -->
            <Button x:Name="MarkerViewerButton"
                    Grid.Column="0"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right" Margin="0,0,6,0"
                    Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Markers (coming soon)">
                <PathIcon Data="M9,0 C5.1,0 2,3.1 2,7 C2,12 9,18 9,18 C9,18 16,12 16,7 C16,3.1 12.9,0 9,0 Z M9,4.5 A2.5,2.5 0 1,0 9,9.5 A2.5,2.5 0 1,0 9,4.5 Z"/>
            </Button>

            <AutoSuggestBox x:Name="PlaceSearchBox"
                            Grid.Column="1"
                            Width="402" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                            PlaceholderText="Search places"
                            QueryIcon="Find"
                            TextMemberPath="Display"
                            Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.PlaceSearch.QueryText, Mode=OneWay}"
                            ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.PlaceSearch.Suggestions}"
                            ItemTemplate="{StaticResource PlaceRowTemplate}"
                            TextChanged="OnPlaceSearchTextChanged"
                            QuerySubmitted="OnPlaceSearchQuerySubmitted"
                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Find a city or town and fly there. Clear the box to remove the pin."/>

            <StackPanel Grid.Column="2"
                        Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="10" Margin="6,0,0,0"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <!-- LOCATION — drop / remove your marker. ONE-WAY IsChecked, re-asserted in the handler. -->
                <ToggleButton x:Name="LocationToggle"
                              Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Markers.CanLocate, Mode=OneWay}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Markers.HasUserLocationMarker, Mode=OneWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind LocationTooltip(ViewModel.Markers.HasUserLocationMarker, ViewModel.Markers.LocateStatusText), Mode=OneWay}"
                              Click="OnToggleUserLocation">
                    <!-- Ring (donut 3.6-5.2), SOLID core (r 2.2), four ticks standing off it. -->
                    <PathIcon Data="M3.8,9 A5.2,5.2 0 1,0 14.2,9 A5.2,5.2 0 1,0 3.8,9 Z M5.4,9 A3.6,3.6 0 1,0 12.6,9 A3.6,3.6 0 1,0 5.4,9 Z M6.8,9 A2.2,2.2 0 1,0 11.2,9 A2.2,2.2 0 1,0 6.8,9 Z M8.2,0 H9.8 V3 H8.2 Z M8.2,15 H9.8 V18 H8.2 Z M0,8.2 H3 V9.8 H0 Z M15,8.2 H18 V9.8 H15 Z"/>
                </ToggleButton>

                <!-- Place search status ("Searching online…", "No places match …"); collapsed when empty. -->
                <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.PlaceSearch.StatusText, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.PlaceSearch.HasStatus, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"/>
            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>

        <!-- ===== MAP TOOLS — RIGHT, over the window keys: pane layout, reset north, fit, isolation ===== -->
        <StackPanel x:Name="RightTools"
                    Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="4"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <!-- PANE LAYOUT — three toggles, current one lit (see the header). Tag = the PaneLayout name. -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="2" Margin="0,0,8,0">
                <ToggleButton x:Name="SinglePaneToggle" Tag="Single"
                              Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind IsSinglePane(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout), Mode=OneWay}"
                              Click="OnPaneLayoutClick"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Activate 1-pane mode">
                    <Grid Width="18" Height="18">
                        <Rectangle Fill="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}" RadiusX="1.5" RadiusY="1.5"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ToggleButton>

                <ToggleButton x:Name="TwoPaneToggle" Tag="TwoAcross"
                              Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind IsTwoPane(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout), Mode=OneWay}"
                              Click="OnPaneLayoutClick"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Activate 2-pane mode">
                    <Grid Width="18" Height="18" ColumnSpacing="2">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition/>
                            <ColumnDefinition/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="0" Fill="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}" RadiusX="1.5" RadiusY="1.5"/>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="1" Fill="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" RadiusX="1.5" RadiusY="1.5"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ToggleButton>

                <ToggleButton x:Name="QuadPaneToggle" Tag="Quad"
                              Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind IsQuadPane(ViewModel.Radar.PaneLayout), Mode=OneWay}"
                              Click="OnPaneLayoutClick"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Activate 4-pane mode">
                    <Grid Width="18" Height="18" ColumnSpacing="2" RowSpacing="2">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition/>
                            <ColumnDefinition/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition/>
                            <RowDefinition/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Fill="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" RadiusX="1" RadiusY="1"/>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Fill="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" RadiusX="1" RadiusY="1"/>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Fill="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefaultBrush}" RadiusX="1" RadiusY="1"/>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Fill="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}" RadiusX="1" RadiusY="1"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ToggleButton>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- Reset north — undo a right-drag rotate/tilt. -->
            <Button Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                    Click="OnResetNorthClick"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Reset North/Flat">
                <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="16" Glyph="&#xE72C;"/>
            </Button>

            <!-- Fit to view — frame the effective region (isolated state, else CONUS). -->
            <Button Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                    Click="OnFitToViewClick"
                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Fit To View">
                <FontIcon FontFamily="Segoe Fluent Icons,Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="16" Glyph="&#xE740;"/>
            </Button>

            <!-- ===== MAP — the basemap's key + its layer flyout (see the header) =====
                 A pair touching at a 1 px seam: the KEY hides/shows the whole basemap, the narrow CAR opens the
                 flyout. Plain TwoWay on the key (a click always flips it). -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="1" Margin="8,0,0,0">
                <ToggleButton x:Name="MapShownToggle"
                              Style="{StaticResource StripToolToggleStyle}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind MapShownTooltip(ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown), Mode=OneWay}">
                    <!-- A folded map: three panels, the middle one set back. Drawn, not an unverified glyph. -->
                    <PathIcon Data="M1,3.6 L5.4,1.8 L5.4,14.6 L1,16.4 Z M6.6,1.8 L11.4,3.6 L11.4,16.4 L6.6,14.6 Z M12.6,3.6 L17,1.8 L17,14.6 L12.6,16.4 Z"/>
                </ToggleButton>
                <Button x:Name="MapLayersButton"
                        Width="16"
                        Style="{StaticResource StripToolButtonStyle}"
                        ToolTipService.ToolTip="Map layers and dimmer">
                    <PathIcon Data="M1,7 L5,3 L9,7 Z"/>
                    <Button.Flyout>
                        <!-- ⚠️ Windowed (ShouldConstrainToRootBounds=False), like the tier's pickers — else the owned
                             panel windows paint over it. -->
                        <Flyout Placement="TopEdgeAlignedRight" ShouldConstrainToRootBounds="False">
                            <StackPanel Width="220" Spacing="2">
                                <TextBlock Text="Map layers" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                                <TextBlock Text="The map is hidden. These apply when you show it."
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12" Margin="0,0,0,4"
                                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"
                                           Visibility="{x:Bind HiddenNoteVisibility(ViewModel.Basemap.IsMapShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
                                <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Basemap.Groups}">
                                    <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:BasemapGroupOption">
                                            <!-- Wrapper carries the tooltip: a disabled CheckBox shows none. -->
                                            <Grid Background="Transparent" ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind ToolTip, Mode=OneWay}">
                                                <CheckBox Content="{x:Bind Label}" MinHeight="32"
                                                          IsChecked="{x:Bind IsShown, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                                          IsEnabled="{x:Bind IsAvailable, Mode=OneWay}"/>
                                            </Grid>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                </ItemsControl>
                                <Grid Margin="0,8,0,0" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                        <ColumnDefinition Width="36"/>
                                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <TextBlock Text="Dim" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                    <Slider Grid.Column="1" Minimum="0" Maximum="90" StepFrequency="5"
                                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                            Value="{x:Bind ViewModel.Basemap.DimPercent, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Fade the basemap toward a blank background"/>
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" VerticalAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                               Text="{x:Bind PercentText(ViewModel.Basemap.DimPercent), Mode=OneWay}"
                                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                                </Grid>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Flyout>
                    </Button.Flyout>
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- ===== STATE ISOLATION — THREE CONTROLS COLLAPSED INTO ONE LIST =====
                 LAST on the right, over the bar's window keys. It replaced the Settings window's Map tab CONUS checkbox,
                 its "isolate a state (hover & click)" arm checkbox, and its state-name combo. One row each:
                 No Isolation / Isolate CONUS / Select to Isolate, then the 52 places.
                 ⚠️ "Select to Isolate" ARMS the map — it is a MODE, not a resting choice. Hovering a state
                 then highlights it, and the click reports back through states.js, at which point the combo
                 re-resolves and reads that state's name. Armed-with-nothing-picked keeps reading "Select to
                 Isolate", which is honest: the map is visibly in hover mode.
                 The three modes are PINNED above a rule and never scroll away; the places scroll below.
                 ⚠️ The PLACEHOLDER should be unreachable: the VM resolves every combination to a real row,
                 "No Isolation" included. Seeing it means the lists failed to build.
                 ⚠⚠ IT IS Primitives/SectionedComboBox, NOT A ComboBox, FOR A CORRECTNESS REASON — a closed
                 WinUI ComboBox cycles its selection on the MOUSEWHEEL, and rolling it here froze the map
                 outright. See that control's header; don't swap it back. -->
            <prim:SectionedComboBox Width="170"
                                    Margin="8,0,0,0"
                                    PlaceholderText="Isolate State"
                                    PinnedItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.IsolationModes, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.IsolationPlaces, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.StateIso.SelectedIsolationOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                    ItemTemplate="{StaticResource IsolationRowTemplate}"
                                    ToolTipService.ToolTip="Mask the map down to CONUS or a single state"/>
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
